1
00:00:22,140 --> 00:00:24,980
The best paradigm

2
00:00:27,060 --> 00:00:30,980
lightly surpassing these hectic times

3
00:00:32,860 --> 00:00:37,460
diving into the city,
playing at being a hero

4
00:00:37,460 --> 00:00:39,440
I wanna dive into paradise

5
00:00:39,440 --> 00:00:42,140
nothing but trendy things

6
00:00:42,140 --> 00:00:45,080
as we keep wearing them

7
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:49,240
because a bare face is
what sells out instantly

8
00:00:49,240 --> 00:00:50,840
Let it ring

9
00:00:50,840 --> 00:00:55,020
Everybody can do, we've started running

10
00:00:55,020 --> 00:00:58,240
Dreams never stop, you know

11
00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:02,480
Let's go regret it again tomorrow

12
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:03,380
Let it run

13
00:01:03,380 --> 00:01:07,680
Everybody can do, just a little

14
00:01:07,680 --> 00:01:10,800
even if we stick out, it doesn't hurt

15
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:15,000
holding onto a noisy curiosity

16
00:01:15,660 --> 00:01:17,280
strong and high

17
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:18,180
Let it run

18
00:01:29,260 --> 00:01:31,740
Recreating the Kyoto trip

19
00:01:37,300 --> 00:01:42,540
Ace

20
00:01:43,420 --> 00:01:44,260
You know him?

21
00:01:44,580 --> 00:01:46,880
Yeah, the cop from the
police box over there, right?

22
00:01:48,020 --> 00:01:49,740
Must be nice, being young.

23
00:01:53,100 --> 00:01:56,580
Looks like those two from the Health
Ministry are here to pick fights again.

24
00:01:56,580 --> 00:01:58,440
Morning, Ryo-chan.

25
00:01:58,440 --> 00:02:00,440
Good morning.

26
00:02:00,440 --> 00:02:02,560
I think it's set to the driver's side.

27
00:02:02,560 --> 00:02:05,420
Don't mind them, seriously,
you don't have to answer.

28
00:02:05,420 --> 00:02:08,440
Ryo-san.

29
00:02:09,700 --> 00:02:13,740
It's probably another interview for that traffic division newsletter,
Green Light, or whatever it's called.

30
00:02:14,740 --> 00:02:16,700
Remember the other day, when I went
to the toilet at the main station too?

31
00:02:17,840 --> 00:02:20,360
Of all times, my hair had to be
a mess right when it was my turn.

32
00:02:26,480 --> 00:02:28,920
From now on,
please go with a softer hairstyle, will you?

33
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:30,780
What do you think you're doing!

34
00:02:30,920 --> 00:02:33,240
The newspaper we worked so hard to make!

35
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:34,600
Insensitive! Barbarian!

36
00:02:34,860 --> 00:02:36,300
That's going too far, Ryo-san.

37
00:02:36,300 --> 00:02:38,480
No, it's an effective form of recycling.

38
00:02:38,480 --> 00:02:39,680
Single-celled organism!

39
00:02:39,900 --> 00:02:42,700
Lower than bacteria and viruses,
you're the worst!

40
00:02:43,160 --> 00:02:43,820
Shut up!

41
00:02:44,740 --> 00:02:48,680
If you have time to make a newspaper with no substance,
go crack down on at least one illegal parking job!

42
00:02:49,100 --> 00:02:50,300
You overpaid thief!

43
00:02:51,100 --> 00:02:52,580
Iiiiiii

44
00:02:52,580 --> 00:02:54,860
Survey of female police
officers in Katsushika

45
00:02:54,860 --> 00:02:56,980
Survey results announced

46
00:02:58,160 --> 00:03:01,000
Number one man you don't want to marry:
Kankichi Ryotsu

47
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:01,340
What?

48
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:04,560
Number one man you don't want as a boss:
Kankichi Ryotsu

49
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:07,760
Number one man you don't want to date:
Kankichi Ryotsu

50
00:03:07,760 --> 00:03:10,020
Number one worst man

51
00:03:10,020 --> 00:03:11,700
Number one beast man

52
00:03:11,700 --> 00:03:13,580
Hopeless men and so on

53
00:03:13,580 --> 00:03:15,840
Worst rankings, all 17 categories

54
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:17,120
Sole first place

55
00:03:17,120 --> 00:03:19,440
Overall top for six
consecutive years goes to

56
00:03:20,300 --> 00:03:20,560
Damn it!

57
00:03:21,120 --> 00:03:22,900
Hohoho! Congratulations!

58
00:03:23,040 --> 00:03:26,700
We'll be running these survey results in Green Light too,
so look forward to it.

59
00:03:27,160 --> 00:03:29,480
Don't publish that crap!
Stop the survey too!

60
00:03:29,580 --> 00:03:30,200
Cut it out!

61
00:03:30,520 --> 00:03:34,040
By the way, the number one man women
want to be held by is Mr. Nakagawa.

62
00:03:34,040 --> 00:03:37,060
And the number one man they'd like
as a big brother was Mr. Terai.

63
00:03:37,060 --> 00:03:38,560
Really?

64
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:39,500
It's true.

65
00:03:40,160 --> 00:03:41,400
What an honor.

66
00:03:41,400 --> 00:03:42,520
Let's combine it with some reporting.

67
00:03:42,520 --> 00:03:44,860
Alright, let's report on the perennial last-place man,
reporting, reporting.

68
00:03:44,860 --> 00:03:45,440
Yes.

69
00:03:46,380 --> 00:03:48,420
Guess I'll go out on patrol.

70
00:03:50,740 --> 00:03:56,360
Right, right, anyway, the reporter said that, didn't he?
Do you remember the mailer?

71
00:03:58,360 --> 00:04:02,580
Senpai, what are you planning to do?
For the interview cooperation?

72
00:04:03,940 --> 00:04:12,200
How dare you mock me! I'll show you everything.
Here, there, and here again, and as a bonus, here too!

73
00:04:12,660 --> 00:04:16,160
That's exactly why you're
the worst one, Senpai.

74
00:04:16,160 --> 00:04:17,340
That's right, that's right!

75
00:04:18,640 --> 00:04:20,780
You idiot, you don't understand how I feel!

76
00:04:20,780 --> 00:04:22,220
Senpai.

77
00:04:22,220 --> 00:04:25,840
I'll openly and fairly make it
clear that this is my message to you.

78
00:04:25,840 --> 00:04:26,520
Annoying.

79
00:04:28,380 --> 00:04:30,320
Hurry up, they're coming!

80
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:33,620
Alright, here we go.

81
00:04:33,620 --> 00:04:34,900
Say cheese!

82
00:04:35,500 --> 00:04:36,280
Win it!

83
00:04:36,280 --> 00:04:38,000
Don't mess with me.

84
00:04:40,960 --> 00:04:43,920
Since I'm already at rock bottom,
there's no fear of falling any further.

85
00:04:43,920 --> 00:04:45,340
It all depends on how you look at it

86
00:04:45,780 --> 00:04:47,500
Thank you for your cooperation.

87
00:04:48,600 --> 00:04:50,220
You're welcome.

88
00:04:51,320 --> 00:04:52,740
The interview's over now.

89
00:04:54,160 --> 00:04:56,500
Nakagawa, Reiko-senpai, sorry for intruding.

90
00:04:56,500 --> 00:04:58,900
Can't forget my important camera.

91
00:04:59,300 --> 00:05:01,180
That's not ours, you know.

92
00:05:04,440 --> 00:05:05,400
Whose is it?

93
00:05:05,400 --> 00:05:07,860
Chief Ohara, good work.

94
00:05:08,860 --> 00:05:11,040
N-no way, the Chief's...

95
00:05:11,040 --> 00:05:13,680
That's my camera, Ryotsu.

96
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:15,560
So I left it here.

97
00:05:15,900 --> 00:05:18,040
I was looking everywhere
for where I'd put it.

98
00:05:18,320 --> 00:05:18,680
Hey.

99
00:05:21,020 --> 00:05:22,040
Well, all of it is fine.

100
00:05:22,160 --> 00:05:23,280
Ryo-chan, what are you going to do?

101
00:05:23,740 --> 00:05:25,200
I'm going to take a little leave.

102
00:05:25,480 --> 00:05:27,620
I'm leaving the rest to you,
Nakagawa, Reiko.

103
00:05:28,060 --> 00:05:29,200
Looks like it's going to be a long one

104
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:31,500
Just five or ten years.

105
00:05:31,720 --> 00:05:32,880
Ryotsu!

106
00:05:35,520 --> 00:05:37,860
Yo-chi, are you in there?

107
00:05:39,120 --> 00:05:41,500
Chief, what's wrong?

108
00:05:41,880 --> 00:05:43,280
Yo-chi, where are you going?

109
00:05:43,420 --> 00:05:46,460
W-well, I was just thinking of
going on patrol or something.

110
00:05:46,460 --> 00:05:48,060
You big idiot!

111
00:05:48,920 --> 00:05:50,980
Go wherever you want!

112
00:05:51,320 --> 00:05:53,020
Don't you dare show me that face again!

113
00:05:53,260 --> 00:05:54,460
You're fired!

114
00:05:54,520 --> 00:05:56,880
I have no use for a vulgar scum like you!

115
00:05:57,000 --> 00:06:00,280
No way, Chief,
there's a deep reason for this...

116
00:06:01,060 --> 00:06:02,800
Chief, you're joking, right?

117
00:06:03,100 --> 00:06:04,260
I'm not joking.

118
00:06:05,400 --> 00:06:10,000
You're fired.
Reiko, you explain everything to them, then.

119
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:10,540
Mm.

120
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:20,440
Nakagawa, Reiko! How could you
two betray me like this, Terai!

121
00:06:21,480 --> 00:06:27,200
Hey, open up! Open this door, or I'll smash it down!
What happens when you make me angry?

122
00:06:27,200 --> 00:06:28,280
Ahahaha!

123
00:06:28,860 --> 00:06:31,360
Reiko-kun, this cake you made is delicious.

124
00:06:31,360 --> 00:06:33,660
If you like, there's plenty more.

125
00:06:36,080 --> 00:06:36,728
Well then,

126
00:06:36,778 --> 00:06:40,620
It's about time you paid back
all the debts you've piled up.

127
00:06:40,620 --> 00:06:44,200
W-wait! I'll definitely pay
you back with my next bonus!

128
00:06:44,780 --> 00:06:46,640
But if I'm fired,
there won't be any bonus...

129
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:47,920
Skater

130
00:06:47,920 --> 00:06:51,680
Nakagawa, Reiko, help me!

131
00:06:54,980 --> 00:06:56,620
So you had it here, Ryotsu!

132
00:06:57,220 --> 00:06:58,760
That's my camera!

133
00:06:59,200 --> 00:06:59,780
Give it back.

134
00:06:59,780 --> 00:07:00,500
Chief.

135
00:07:00,500 --> 00:07:03,340
Nice camera.

136
00:07:03,340 --> 00:07:04,960
It's a Nikon F50, isn't it?

137
00:07:04,960 --> 00:07:06,540
I've been wanting one, too.

138
00:07:06,540 --> 00:07:07,880
Your eye for quality is as sharp as ever.

139
00:07:08,960 --> 00:07:10,280
It's a camera I'm not used to, you see.

140
00:07:10,280 --> 00:07:12,340
and I never figured out
how to take the film out.

141
00:07:12,340 --> 00:07:14,040
Looks like I carried it
around and forgot about it.

142
00:07:15,540 --> 00:07:16,260
I see.

143
00:07:17,960 --> 00:07:19,260
Well, that's good, that's good.

144
00:07:19,260 --> 00:07:20,520
I had a feeling, but I didn't think...

145
00:07:20,520 --> 00:07:22,260
that you'd left it at the police box.

146
00:07:23,840 --> 00:07:25,740
If that gets found out,
it's a caught-in-the-act offense, you know.

147
00:07:27,500 --> 00:07:29,560
We're sending it out for developing,
so hand it back quickly.

148
00:07:29,560 --> 00:07:30,600
Developing it is a bit...

149
00:07:31,400 --> 00:07:32,980
Don't be so persistent, Ryotsu!

150
00:07:32,980 --> 00:07:33,700
Ah.

151
00:07:38,040 --> 00:07:39,120
W-wait, you can't be serious.

152
00:07:39,540 --> 00:07:40,440
I'm not joking.

153
00:07:40,800 --> 00:07:42,360
You're fired.

154
00:07:42,360 --> 00:07:44,240
W-wait, please, just a moment.

155
00:07:44,240 --> 00:07:45,720
Where do you plan to take it?

156
00:07:46,060 --> 00:07:48,520
It's Pikarika Camera in
the shopping arcade, but...

157
00:07:48,520 --> 00:07:50,040
Not there. That place is no good.

158
00:07:50,040 --> 00:07:53,360
In this day and age,
they charge twenty yen per print?!

159
00:07:53,360 --> 00:07:54,600
They're taking consumers for fools.

160
00:07:54,980 --> 00:07:57,440
Is there a cheaper shop somewhere?

161
00:07:57,440 --> 00:08:00,860
Yes, I know a shop where
printing costs zero yen.

162
00:08:00,860 --> 00:08:03,660
Don't lie.
Can a business really run on zero yen?

163
00:08:03,660 --> 00:08:08,360
It can. The materials cost for
one 24-exposure roll is 600 yen.

164
00:08:08,360 --> 00:08:13,660
The most expensive part is the printing paper,
about 30%, or 180 yen.

165
00:08:13,660 --> 00:08:17,500
Even if you deduct 40% for other overhead,
like chemicals and labor,

166
00:08:17,500 --> 00:08:21,900
the remaining 30%,
or 180 yen, is booked as profit.

167
00:08:21,900 --> 00:08:23,080
Fine.

168
00:08:23,080 --> 00:08:27,140
Those photos are due to the
traffic division tomorrow.

169
00:08:27,140 --> 00:08:28,880
Get them there by 10 a.m.

170
00:08:28,880 --> 00:08:29,880
Leave it to me.

171
00:08:29,880 --> 00:08:32,560
I'll bring them by 10 tomorrow,
without fail.

172
00:08:39,580 --> 00:08:43,100
With a color developing kit like this,
it's not that hard.

173
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:45,900
Just cut out the parts where the feet show.

174
00:08:47,940 --> 00:08:50,620
Excuse me, could you grab the ball?

175
00:09:21,740 --> 00:09:30,160
If I had to guess, you probably went around snapping postcard-style photos of Kyoto's famous sights,
with no people in them.

176
00:09:30,160 --> 00:09:39,280
I don't remember what I shot anyway. Copies of postcards will be enough to fool them.
Will it really work? Don't worry, they won't find out.

177
00:09:43,320 --> 00:09:46,920
Hello, this is Kameari Park police box.
Is Ryotsu there?

178
00:09:48,020 --> 00:09:49,440
Yes, Chief, what is it?

179
00:09:49,440 --> 00:09:50,400
Is that Ryotsu?

180
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:53,360
I forgot to say, make the prints big.

181
00:09:53,360 --> 00:09:57,340
I took it standing next to the
most beautiful maiko in Kyoto.

182
00:09:57,860 --> 00:09:59,280
W-wait, you took it standing next to her?

183
00:09:59,860 --> 00:10:02,120
The General Affairs
bonus chief took it for me.

184
00:10:02,120 --> 00:10:03,620
It might end up in the newspaper.

185
00:10:03,620 --> 00:10:05,240
It's an important photo, so.

186
00:10:05,240 --> 00:10:07,640
Make it clear and crisp, Ryotsu.

187
00:10:07,640 --> 00:10:09,400
Sure, sure, leave it to me.

188
00:10:11,460 --> 00:10:12,760
So I'm fired?

189
00:10:12,760 --> 00:10:13,840
You're fired.

190
00:10:15,300 --> 00:10:17,060
Postcards alone won't get you out of this.

191
00:10:17,440 --> 00:10:20,960
Bad CG compositing gets
spotted right away these days.

192
00:10:21,980 --> 00:10:23,920
It's your fault.
Let's do something about this.

193
00:10:23,920 --> 00:10:26,080
I have nothing to do with it.

194
00:10:26,080 --> 00:10:29,620
This happened because you took a
picture of my face in the first place!

195
00:10:29,620 --> 00:10:31,480
But that was Senpai's doing!

196
00:10:31,480 --> 00:10:34,180
If I'm getting fired, you're coming with me.

197
00:10:34,820 --> 00:10:37,200
What a foolish police career it was,
Nakagawa.

198
00:10:38,460 --> 00:10:39,100
Understood.

199
00:10:53,740 --> 00:10:57,580
Bonus Chief!

200
00:10:57,940 --> 00:10:58,680
That's unreasonable!

201
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:03,040
You remember the photo we took
with Chief Ohara in Kyoto, right?

202
00:11:03,620 --> 00:11:05,520
That was last week, though.

203
00:11:05,960 --> 00:11:08,800
Then I want you to
reproduce it crisp and clear.

204
00:11:09,340 --> 00:11:09,700
Yes.

205
00:11:10,480 --> 00:11:11,260
How's this?

206
00:11:11,640 --> 00:11:13,980
I've sent all the data about the chief.

207
00:11:14,640 --> 00:11:16,600
All that's left is the
clothes he wore that day.

208
00:11:18,800 --> 00:11:20,000
Hey, this is crap. Total crap.

209
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:24,360
I think it was brown
dye and a necktie, right?

210
00:11:24,820 --> 00:11:25,000
Yes.

211
00:11:26,920 --> 00:11:28,400
That's it, that's it. The color is...

212
00:11:28,400 --> 00:11:31,780
Crisp and clear...

213
00:11:31,780 --> 00:11:33,760
This color is close.

214
00:11:33,760 --> 00:11:35,980
Yes, that's exactly it.

215
00:11:35,980 --> 00:11:36,820
Good job!

216
00:11:36,820 --> 00:11:40,600
After that, tomorrow, our company's
staff will be preparing and waiting for it.

217
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:41,920
It should be fine somehow.

218
00:12:01,840 --> 00:12:03,780
So we finally made it.

219
00:12:13,340 --> 00:12:15,140
Chief.

220
00:12:19,640 --> 00:12:21,440
Chief.

221
00:12:21,440 --> 00:12:22,720
When did this happen?

222
00:12:22,720 --> 00:12:23,620
Senpai.

223
00:12:23,620 --> 00:12:24,160
Yeah.

224
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:31,220
It's a doll, Senpai.
If you're fooled, it's perfect.

225
00:12:38,900 --> 00:12:49,400
The color, sheen, and texture are so well done you'd never think it's a doll.
It's foam latex, the kind used in special effects. Unless you look up close, you can't tell.

226
00:12:49,920 --> 00:12:50,499
This face,

227
00:12:50,549 --> 00:12:54,640
when the Chief stands in front of a camera,
he gets nervous and always makes this face.

228
00:12:54,640 --> 00:12:57,820
But why would they go to the
trouble of making something like this?

229
00:12:58,340 --> 00:12:59,780
Let's not ask unnecessary questions.

230
00:13:00,360 --> 00:13:03,020
But, young master, it's ready.

231
00:13:03,020 --> 00:13:06,560
Senpai, the staff who'll help
with the shoot have arrived.

232
00:13:19,560 --> 00:13:20,480
Aaaaaah.

233
00:13:20,480 --> 00:13:21,920
Aaaaaah.

234
00:13:27,100 --> 00:13:28,340
Is this everyone?

235
00:13:33,280 --> 00:13:34,320
Uncle.

236
00:13:35,400 --> 00:13:38,740
We've narrowed it down,
and I think this maiko is the one.

237
00:13:38,740 --> 00:13:41,960
Welcome, it's been a week.

238
00:13:42,740 --> 00:13:43,820
That one from back then.

239
00:13:44,460 --> 00:13:46,960
Alright, the cast is all here.
Let's start the shoot!

240
00:14:00,940 --> 00:14:01,640
How's this?

241
00:14:02,200 --> 00:14:04,520
That's exactly the feel of the light.

242
00:14:04,520 --> 00:14:06,180
Good, go ahead and shoot.

243
00:14:06,180 --> 00:14:07,460
Here we go, I'm shooting.

244
00:14:10,400 --> 00:14:11,800
Next, the camera.

245
00:14:18,800 --> 00:14:20,860
Lately, our special effects staff

246
00:14:20,860 --> 00:14:22,720
have been working on computer graphics

247
00:14:22,720 --> 00:14:24,760
on a huge rendering production, you know.

248
00:14:25,260 --> 00:14:27,200
Dinosaurs, tornadoes,
that sort of thing, right?

249
00:14:27,800 --> 00:14:28,120
Yeah.

250
00:14:28,960 --> 00:14:30,940
Well, at this rate, by evening

251
00:14:30,940 --> 00:14:32,300
we should be able to
get back to the station.

252
00:14:32,300 --> 00:14:33,600
Sorry to keep you waiting.

253
00:14:34,660 --> 00:14:35,800
Please, take your time.

254
00:14:35,800 --> 00:14:37,120
Go ahead and eat.

255
00:14:37,660 --> 00:14:39,460
I thought it was location bento,

256
00:14:39,460 --> 00:14:41,940
but a dining car too? That's amazing.

257
00:14:41,940 --> 00:14:44,060
On American location shoots,
that's standard.

258
00:14:48,080 --> 00:14:49,300
This is delicious.

259
00:14:50,440 --> 00:14:52,340
He used to work at the
Sheraton in Hong Kong,

260
00:14:52,340 --> 00:14:55,200
where he was executive chef. I poached him.

261
00:14:56,020 --> 00:14:57,820
Where should we put the Chief?

262
00:14:58,860 --> 00:15:01,420
That's why Chief Ohara took
the photos of the ducks.

263
00:15:01,420 --> 00:15:02,760
I'm not going into the river.

264
00:15:03,260 --> 00:15:04,280
You should have said that sooner!

265
00:15:04,280 --> 00:15:05,560
No Chief.

266
00:15:05,940 --> 00:15:07,680
I think it's where the ducks fly.

267
00:15:14,520 --> 00:15:15,140
What's wrong?

268
00:15:15,720 --> 00:15:17,700
Wasn't it the one where
he was bathing outdoors?

269
00:15:18,740 --> 00:15:19,920
Hey, it's the outdoor bath one.

270
00:15:21,940 --> 00:15:23,540
Wasn't it the piggyback one?

271
00:15:24,780 --> 00:15:26,240
Piggyback, piggyback.

272
00:15:27,720 --> 00:15:28,660
That's impossible.

273
00:15:28,660 --> 00:15:30,900
I feel like it wasn't a duck...

274
00:15:30,900 --> 00:15:33,100
Enough already.

275
00:15:33,100 --> 00:15:35,160
Remember it clearly, will you?

276
00:15:36,860 --> 00:15:38,040
If you push him like that...

277
00:15:38,040 --> 00:15:40,020
He won't remember anything at this rate.

278
00:15:41,020 --> 00:15:44,980
Carp, it's carp.
Three carp, no doubt about it.

279
00:15:45,300 --> 00:15:46,900
Carp. Get the carp ready.

280
00:15:56,700 --> 00:15:57,460
How is it?

281
00:15:57,680 --> 00:15:59,400
Yes, it looks fine.

282
00:16:05,100 --> 00:16:06,640
Right, make the waves fall.

283
00:16:16,360 --> 00:16:16,980
Wind!

284
00:16:26,760 --> 00:16:28,320
The chief's flying!

285
00:16:39,020 --> 00:16:41,620
Alright, one more shot and we're home free.

286
00:16:47,980 --> 00:16:51,460
Hey, stop dawdling and hurry
up and press the shutter!

287
00:16:51,460 --> 00:16:55,460
Back then,
the kanzakura behind us was in full bloom,

288
00:16:55,460 --> 00:16:57,280
so make the cherry blossoms bloom fully.

289
00:16:57,280 --> 00:16:57,740
Yes.

290
00:17:03,660 --> 00:17:06,540
And there were about fifty
people from a senior tour group,

291
00:17:06,540 --> 00:17:08,240
so fifty senior extras.

292
00:17:08,240 --> 00:17:08,640
Hey.

293
00:17:15,260 --> 00:17:18,100
And the sky was a sunset
as far as the eye could see.

294
00:17:18,100 --> 00:17:18,760
You idiot!

295
00:17:19,340 --> 00:17:20,500
Don't tell me this after
it's already getting dark!

296
00:17:20,500 --> 00:17:21,280
Sorry.

297
00:17:21,880 --> 00:17:23,100
Can you make a sunset?

298
00:17:24,020 --> 00:17:25,680
I don't think so, not in this darkness.

299
00:17:25,680 --> 00:17:27,240
We'll try our best somehow.

300
00:17:51,200 --> 00:17:53,720
This is it,
this is the sunset from that day.

301
00:17:53,720 --> 00:17:55,060
Hurry up and take the shot.

302
00:17:55,060 --> 00:17:55,360
Yes.

303
00:17:58,960 --> 00:18:00,720
Well, we got through it somehow.

304
00:18:00,720 --> 00:18:03,220
You've had a rough time too, haven't you.

305
00:18:03,220 --> 00:18:04,340
Good work, you two.

306
00:18:06,960 --> 00:18:08,680
Even without tearing each other down,

307
00:18:08,680 --> 00:18:09,560
Shut up.

308
00:18:09,560 --> 00:18:12,860
Even though they're just dolls,
thinking about having two Chief Oharas,

309
00:18:12,860 --> 00:18:13,980
it gives me the creeps.

310
00:18:14,340 --> 00:18:16,880
Platform 12, 21:34

311
00:18:16,880 --> 00:18:19,580
Nozomi 304 bound for Tokyo

312
00:18:19,580 --> 00:18:21,700
We somehow made it onto
the last bullet train.

313
00:18:22,260 --> 00:18:24,500
This gets us to Tokyo
Station before midnight.

314
00:18:24,500 --> 00:18:25,840
Once we get back, develop these.

315
00:18:25,840 --> 00:18:27,260
Piece of cake.

316
00:18:29,840 --> 00:18:30,520
W-what?

317
00:18:31,580 --> 00:18:33,180
There was one more photo.

318
00:18:33,640 --> 00:18:33,980
What?

319
00:18:34,700 --> 00:18:37,700
We forgot the photo of the
most important Buddhist statue!

320
00:18:37,700 --> 00:18:39,200
Wait a minute!

321
00:18:42,180 --> 00:18:43,780
Yes, yes, I understand.

322
00:18:44,340 --> 00:18:45,020
It's no good.

323
00:18:45,020 --> 00:18:46,620
The film crew just now

324
00:18:46,620 --> 00:18:49,020
apparently all left for the Alaska location.

325
00:18:49,020 --> 00:18:49,860
Then what about the helicopter?

326
00:18:49,860 --> 00:18:52,580
It's stuck in Nagoya with engine trouble.

327
00:18:52,580 --> 00:18:54,760
It doesn't look like it can
fly for two or three hours.

328
00:18:54,760 --> 00:18:55,380
Damn it.

329
00:18:57,380 --> 00:18:58,000
So that's the only option

330
00:19:00,320 --> 00:19:02,280
Senpai, did you find any?

331
00:19:06,320 --> 00:19:08,340
How far are you going to

332
00:19:08,340 --> 00:19:09,940
go just to make me suffer?

333
00:19:14,160 --> 00:19:15,860
Senpai, are you all right?

334
00:19:18,320 --> 00:19:20,160
Open up, open up!

335
00:19:20,680 --> 00:19:21,840
Show us the Buddhist statue.

336
00:19:22,780 --> 00:19:23,960
Open the door, please.

337
00:19:24,820 --> 00:19:25,380
Hey!

338
00:19:27,380 --> 00:19:30,680
This isn't just an ordinary Buddhist statue,
you know.

339
00:19:31,100 --> 00:19:34,280
It's only been opened to the public once in a thousand years,
and only for three minutes.

340
00:19:34,280 --> 00:19:36,860
Because it's a super
royal-class Buddhist statue.

341
00:19:36,860 --> 00:19:37,800
Show us the statue.

342
00:19:37,800 --> 00:19:39,800
What business do you have
at this hour of the night?

343
00:19:39,800 --> 00:19:41,400
Please show us this Buddhist statue.

344
00:19:41,840 --> 00:19:44,080
We only show this once in a thousand years.

345
00:19:44,080 --> 00:19:45,520
Don't call me Mimi-chi.

346
00:19:45,980 --> 00:19:47,360
Bingo, the real thing!

347
00:19:53,580 --> 00:19:54,300
Are you all right?

348
00:19:54,300 --> 00:19:58,120
Damn it, this way won't work! If it comes to this,
I'll sneak in no matter what!

349
00:20:08,740 --> 00:20:11,532
Senpai, this is really bad, you know.

350
00:20:11,582 --> 00:20:13,320
Isn't this trespassing?

351
00:20:13,660 --> 00:20:15,160
This is no time for that!

352
00:20:15,420 --> 00:20:17,000
Who's there! Who's over there!

353
00:20:17,480 --> 00:20:18,360
S-senpai!

354
00:20:18,480 --> 00:20:19,180
Alright, seriously!

355
00:20:19,580 --> 00:20:20,600
Just run!

356
00:20:24,300 --> 00:20:25,680
Aaaaaah!

357
00:20:25,680 --> 00:20:26,760
Aaaaaah!

358
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:48,160
Security's too tight, there's no way. Giving up after coming all this way...
But if the next time we can see it is a thousand years from now...

359
00:20:50,080 --> 00:20:52,180
Did you come up with some good idea?

360
00:20:52,780 --> 00:20:54,960
Now that's an option.

361
00:20:54,960 --> 00:20:55,420
Yes.

362
00:20:56,180 --> 00:20:56,980
What?

363
00:21:12,960 --> 00:21:13,840
Damn it.

364
00:21:13,840 --> 00:21:16,800
Why do we have to do even this?

365
00:21:18,320 --> 00:21:20,440
Hey, it looks exactly like him, senpai.

366
00:21:20,680 --> 00:21:21,320
I see.

367
00:21:21,880 --> 00:21:23,940
Hahaha. Right, we're short on time.

368
00:21:24,080 --> 00:21:24,420
Yes.

369
00:21:24,820 --> 00:21:26,860
Ugh, come on, let's just get the shot.

370
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:28,800
Yes. First, turn around,

371
00:21:28,850 --> 00:21:31,840
put your body into it, and face this way.

372
00:21:34,260 --> 00:21:37,600
Right arm from the back of
the neck to the left cheek,

373
00:21:37,600 --> 00:21:40,200
and the fingers are in the mouth, right?

374
00:21:40,800 --> 00:21:41,780
Like this.

375
00:21:41,780 --> 00:21:46,460
Looking closely, he's in a seated meditation pose,
balanced on the big toe of one foot.

376
00:21:48,840 --> 00:21:53,180
The left arm comes from inside the
crossed legs and reaches toward the nostril.

377
00:21:53,180 --> 00:21:56,720
The right eye glares northeast,
and the left eye glares southwest.

378
00:21:57,780 --> 00:21:59,100
Hurry up and take it.

379
00:22:00,260 --> 00:22:01,320
Okay, I'm taking it.

380
00:22:12,600 --> 00:22:13,960
We made it!

381
00:22:23,600 --> 00:22:25,880
Ryo-chan still hasn't come back, has he?

382
00:22:25,880 --> 00:22:26,980
Yeah, that's right.

383
00:22:26,980 --> 00:22:31,480
Did the shoot come in? Well, about that...

384
00:22:32,060 --> 00:22:34,740
We finished shooting!

385
00:22:35,860 --> 00:22:44,420
Yeah, I put the film in, but that camera was so heavy that right before we left I switched to this one.
I completely forgot, apparently?

386
00:22:44,420 --> 00:22:44,840
Well then,

387
00:22:44,840 --> 00:22:46,100
Aaaah!

388
00:22:47,300 --> 00:22:48,340
They're done!

389
00:22:49,060 --> 00:22:49,800
Whoa!

390
00:22:51,640 --> 00:22:54,230
Chief, the photos are ready!

391
00:22:54,600 --> 00:22:56,600
Y-you! Is that Ryotsu?

392
00:22:56,720 --> 00:22:57,320
Ryo-chan?

393
00:22:57,700 --> 00:22:58,780
How come he looks so cool?

394
00:22:58,780 --> 00:23:01,780
Look, look at this! It's the Chief's photo!

395
00:23:01,780 --> 00:23:02,860
A photo?

396
00:23:04,800 --> 00:23:05,720
W-what's this?

397
00:23:08,640 --> 00:23:10,400
There are two of me!

398
00:23:10,400 --> 00:23:12,080
W-what is this?

399
00:23:12,320 --> 00:23:14,520
Even the poses are exactly the same.

400
00:23:14,520 --> 00:23:17,620
But it looks like there are
slight differences in the details.

401
00:23:17,620 --> 00:23:18,860
What is the meaning of this?

402
00:23:18,860 --> 00:23:21,460
Ryotsu, you're up to something again,
aren't you?

403
00:23:21,460 --> 00:23:23,600
Chief...

404
00:23:24,980 --> 00:23:27,060
Yes! The definitive photo!

405
00:23:27,060 --> 00:23:29,300
Look forward to the next green light.

406
00:23:29,300 --> 00:23:31,000
Damn you bastards!

407
00:23:34,140 --> 00:23:35,100
Uh-oh.

408
00:23:35,100 --> 00:23:38,700
Let's hear your side of the story, Ryotsu.

409
00:23:38,700 --> 00:23:40,420
Chief, wait, please!

410
00:23:40,420 --> 00:23:42,340
There's a deep reason behind this.

411
00:24:06,080 --> 00:24:08,400
Gourmet critic Chōho Ōmaeda

412
00:24:08,400 --> 00:24:11,580
Countless shops have nearly gone under
because of this guy's careless reviews.

413
00:24:12,340 --> 00:24:13,880
Your grudge is a terrifying thing!

414
00:24:14,080 --> 00:24:15,500
Next, I'm the one you'll face!

415
00:24:15,600 --> 00:24:16,920
Come at me!

416
00:24:18,000 --> 00:24:21,540
Next time: the soba shop rebuilding plan.
See you then!

417
00:24:29,580 --> 00:24:32,660
Even if you try to stop the clock,

418
00:24:35,020 --> 00:24:37,720
time keeps moving on.

419
00:24:39,320 --> 00:24:48,020
Frowning and crying,
laughing it off, let's keep living.

420
00:24:50,340 --> 00:25:03,440
Even if today is rainy,
tomorrow will be sunny.

421
00:25:03,440 --> 00:25:13,860
Bye-bye, let's wave goodbye,
unpleasant things, farewell!

422
00:25:13,860 --> 00:25:23,980
Oh yeah, let's try living as we like,
good things will come.

423
00:25:23,980 --> 00:25:30,260
Outside the door, the stars are calling you.

424
00:25:35,980 --> 00:25:41,040
Thank you for watching.

